{"page":794,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.42424,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"780 Chapter 13: Vector-Valued Functions and Motion in Space"},{"x":0.17902,"y":0.10125,"w":0.01753,"h":0.02562,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"d2s dt2"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.10835,"w":0.44855,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Formula for Calculating the Normal Component of Acceleration"},{"x":0.55363,"y":0.12086,"w":0.12231,"h":0.02776,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"aN = 20 a0 2 - aT"},{"x":0.67804,"y":0.13253,"w":0.20395,"h":0.01421,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 (3)"},{"x":0.18244,"y":0.14756,"w":0.08413,"h":0.0227,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"k0 v0 2N = N r 0 v0 2"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.18333,"w":0.52885,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 1 Without finding T and N, write the acceleration of the motion"},{"x":0.43801,"y":0.20737,"w":0.35956,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"r(t) = (cos t + t sin t)i + (sin t - t cos t)j, t 7 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.23039,"w":0.59304,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"in the form a = aTT + aNN. (The path of the motion is the involute of the circle in Figure 13.27. See also Section 13.3, Exercise 19.)"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.27417,"w":0.25434,"h":0.07367,"fs":0.01151,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 13.26 The tangential and normal components of the acceleration of an object that is speeding up as it moves counterclockwise around a circle of radius r."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.27626,"w":0.35862,"h":0.01517,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution We use the first of Equations (2) to find aT:"},{"x":0.4036,"y":0.29803,"w":0.04803,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"v = dr"},{"x":0.43756,"y":0.30457,"w":0.3944,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dt = (-sin t + sin t + t cos t)i + (cos t - cos t + t sin t)j"},{"x":0.41902,"y":0.32759,"w":0.14825,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= (t cos t)i + (t sin t)j"},{"x":0.39448,"y":0.34459,"w":0.36275,"h":0.02588,"fs":0.01353,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"0 v0 = 2t2 cos2t + t2 sin2t = 2t2 = 0 t0 = t t 7 0"},{"x":0.43626,"y":0.37145,"w":0.0696,"h":0.03315,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dt 0 v0 = d"},{"x":0.39694,"y":0.37733,"w":0.04976,"h":0.02188,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"aT = d"},{"x":0.49544,"y":0.38386,"w":0.26677,"h":0.02076,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dt (t) = 1. Eq. (2)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.41266,"w":0.2931,"h":0.01433,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Knowing aT, we use Equation (3) to find aN:"},{"x":0.46728,"y":0.43118,"w":0.41766,"h":0.03393,"fs":0.01353,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"a = (cos t - t sin t)i + (sin t + t cos t)j 0 a0 2 = t2 + 1 After some algebra"},{"x":0.20949,"y":0.43425,"w":0.04092,"h":0.02404,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"T a"},{"x":0.47464,"y":0.46225,"w":0.12231,"h":0.02776,"fs":0.01353,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"aN = 20 a0 2 - aT"},{"x":0.22003,"y":0.4706,"w":0.08151,"h":0.01585,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"P(x, y) tN"},{"x":0.15652,"y":0.49191,"w":0.0345,"h":0.02016,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"String"},{"x":0.49836,"y":0.49321,"w":0.21662,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"= 2(t2 + 1) - (1) = 2t2 = t."},{"x":0.10466,"y":0.51713,"w":0.12281,"h":0.01146,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Q r"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.52136,"w":0.22963,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"We then use Equation (1) to find a:"},{"x":0.46952,"y":0.54372,"w":0.29654,"h":0.01499,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"a = aTT + aNN = (1)T + (t)N = T + tN."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.57346,"w":0.05439,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Torsion"},{"x":0.23461,"y":0.58036,"w":0.06597,"h":0.0173,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"(1, 0) x"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.58768,"w":0.59297,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"How does dB>ds behave in relation to T, N, and B? From the rule for differentiating a cross product in Section 13.1, we have"},{"x":0.21392,"y":0.6204,"w":0.06811,"h":0.01461,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"x2 + y2 = 1"},{"x":0.48161,"y":0.63415,"w":0.10792,"h":0.03007,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ds = d(T * N)"},{"x":0.61679,"y":0.63686,"w":0.13416,"h":0.02736,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ds * N + T * dN"},{"x":0.47888,"y":0.63694,"w":0.02004,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dB"},{"x":0.5492,"y":0.63694,"w":0.08489,"h":0.02728,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"ds = dT"},{"x":0.73322,"y":0.64416,"w":0.02356,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ds ."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.66441,"w":0.38092,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Since N is the direction of dT>ds, (dT>ds) * N = 0 and"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.67618,"w":0.23733,"h":0.04298,"fs":0.01151,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 13.27 The tangential and normal components of the acceleration of the motion r(t) = (cos t + t sin t)i +"},{"x":0.51067,"y":0.69824,"w":0.1305,"h":0.02736,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ds = 0 + T * dN"},{"x":0.62344,"y":0.69824,"w":0.09845,"h":0.02736,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ds = T * dN"},{"x":0.50794,"y":0.69833,"w":0.02003,"h":0.0128,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dB"},{"x":0.70416,"y":0.70555,"w":0.02356,"h":0.02008,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ds ."},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.72238,"w":0.24125,"h":0.0735,"fs":0.01151,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"(sin t - t cos t)j, for t 7 0. If a string wound around a fixed circle is unwound while held taut in the plane of the circle, its end P traces an involute of the circle (Example 1)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.7258,"w":0.59299,"h":0.03858,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"From this we see that dB>ds is orthogonal to T, since a cross product is orthogonal to its factors."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.75649,"w":0.59308,"h":0.05392,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Since dB>ds is also orthogonal to B (the latter has constant length), it follows that dB>ds is orthogonal to the plane of B and T. In other words, dB>ds is parallel to N, so dB>ds is a scalar multiple of N. In symbols,"},{"x":0.57846,"y":0.81599,"w":0.01907,"h":0.0128,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dB"},{"x":0.58071,"y":0.82252,"w":0.0765,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"ds = -tN."},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.84554,"w":0.59299,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"The negative sign in this equation is traditional. The scalar t is called the torsion along the curve. Notice that"},{"x":0.50476,"y":0.88327,"w":0.2284,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ds # N = -tN # N = -t(1) = -t."},{"x":0.50251,"y":0.88505,"w":0.01907,"h":0.0128,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dB"},{"x":0.32334,"y":0.92296,"w":0.288,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"We use this equation for our next definition."}]}